<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Feb 24.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Feb 24.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    387.30   2.44</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	   295.83   1.42</p>
<p> 3   Mt Edon Gold	   241.76   2.20</p>
<p> 4   Niugini Min	    235.25   3.27</p>
<p> 5   Mayne Nickless	 166.45   7.54</p>
<p> 6   ST.Barbara Mine	129.58   0.92</p>
<p> 7   Adel Bton Cement     126.09   1.74</p>
<p> 8   Colonial Coml	  125.68   2.30</p>
<p> 9   Westpac Prop Tr	108.12   1.73</p>
<p>10   Herald Rsc	     101.77   1.15</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     2.16   0.94</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    4.12   1.00</p>
<p> 3   BTR Plc		    6.02   5.60</p>
<p> 4   Premier Inv		6.48   1.15</p>
